        "subject": "LU-18941 tests: fix sanity/119j RPC count races",
        "message": "LU-18941 tests: fix sanity/119j RPC count races\n\nsanity test_119j intermittently fails on aarch64/64K-page clients\n(~25% of runs) with both \"(3) 1 != 0 read RPCs\" and \"(5)/(7)\n0 != 1 read RPCs\".  The landed read-size fix did not help because\nthe failures are RPC-count races, not read-size mismatches.\n\nLU-19344 (\"llite: set read size correctly\") reordered\ndo_file_read_iter() so ll_do_fast_read() now runs before the hybrid\nBIO->DIO switch check, unlike the write path where the switch is\nevaluated before the (guarded) tiny-write fast path.  As a result,\nwhen OBD_FAIL_LLITE_FORCE_BIO_AS_DIO is set, the forced-DIO read is\nonly sent to the server if its pages are actually cold; otherwise\nfast read serves it from cache and no RPC is generated.  The test\nrelied on \"sysctl -w vm.drop_caches=3\" to cool the cache, but that\nis best-effort and does not reliably evict pages pinned by OSC DLM\nlocks, which is racier on large-page clients.\n\nUse cancel_lru_locks osc to deterministically invalidate the file's\ncached pages before the forced-DIO read and write, so the IO is a\ntrue cache miss.  Also add a warm-up read before the cached-read\nmeasurement so a first-touch asynchronous readahead RPC cannot race\nthe stats reset and be miscounted (the \"(3) 1 != 0\" failure).  Fix\nthe stale \"read RPCs\" text in the write check.\n\nFixes: 240cad9a0a (\"LU-19344 llite: set read size correctly\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=119j,ONLY_REPEAT=20\nSigned-off-by: Robert Read <rread@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: If79520dc6a17c40c3767692bdadbf5be8f5caf78\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66703\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Shaun Tancheff <shaun.tancheff@hpe.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
